content.text:
Now index.css cp- block. Append at end of index.css.

Design tokens + classes:

```css
/* ==========================================================================
   Console tokens and surfaces (cp): the E2 instrument panel.
   Reuses the rp palette as custom properties, adds one hue per verdict
   band, and keeps every interactive target at 44px or larger.
   ========================================================================== */

:root {
  --cp-ground: var(--rp-void);
  --cp-surface: var(--rp-panel);
  --cp-surface-strong: var(--rp-panel-strong);
  --cp-rule: var(--rp-rule);
  --cp-ink: var(--rp-paper);
  --cp-ink-dim: var(--rp-text-dim);
  --cp-ink-faint: var(--rp-text-faint);
  --cp-band-critical: #ff6a4d;
  --cp-band-storm: #f4b740;
  --cp-band-watch: #8b7cf6;
  --cp-band-fair: #39c2e0;
  --cp-band-clear: #35d0ae;
  --cp-radius: var(--rp-radius);
}
```

Shell:
```css
.cp-shell { display: grid; gap: var(--rp-s4); }
.cp-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--rp-s4); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: start; }
@media (min-width: 64rem) { .cp-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr); } }
```

Panel:
```css
.cp-panel { background: var(--cp-surface); border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-radius: var(--cp-radius); padding: var(--rp-s5); }
.cp-panel__head { margin-bottom: var(--rp-s4); }
.cp-eyebrow { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--rp-verified); margin: 0; }
.cp-eyebrow--alert { color: var(--rp-stamp); }
.cp-title { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.2vw, 1.6rem); letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.15; margin: var(--rp-s1) 0 var(--rp-s2); color: var(--cp-ink); }
```
Careful: letter-spacing: -0.02em — negative letter spacing is fine (not a dash character) ✓. But my dash scan test only scans TS files, not CSS ✓.

Hmm wait: does the content rule about dashes apply to CSS? "in ANY string you write (UI copy, comments, docs)". CSS letter-spacing -0.02em is a value, not a dash character in copy. It's a minus sign character "-"? It's the ASCII hyphen in a numeric value — like numeric minus, allowed. Fine.

Continue:
```css
.cp-sub { font-size: .8125rem; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); margin: 0; }
.cp-label { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); display: block; }
.cp-hint { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); margin: var(--rp-s3) 0 0; }
.cp-status { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.0625rem; color: var(--cp-ink); margin: var(--rp-s2) 0 0; }
```

Lookup:
```css
.cp-lookup__row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--rp-s2); margin-top: var(--rp-s2); }
.cp-input { flex: 1 1 14rem; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 var(--rp-s3); background: rgba(7,12,24,.6); border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-radius: var(--cp-radius); color: var(--cp-ink); font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-size: 1rem; letter-spacing: .06em; }
.cp-input::placeholder { color: var(--cp-ink-faint); letter-spacing: normal; }
.cp-input:focus-visible, .cp-slider:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--rp-paper); outline-offset: 2px; }
.cp-suggestions { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--rp-s2); margin: var(--rp-s3) 0 0; padding: 0; }
.cp-suggestion { min-height: 44px; min-width: 5.5rem; padding: 0 var(--rp-s3); border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-radius: var(--cp-radius); background: rgba(7,12,24,.5); color: var(--cp-ink); font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-size: .9375rem; cursor: pointer; }
.cp-suggestion:hover { border-color: var(--rp-verified); }
.cp-suggestion[aria-pressed='true'] { background: var(--rp-verified-ghost); border-color: var(--rp-verified); color: var(--rp-verified); }
```

Button:
```css
.cp-button { min-height: 44px; padding: 0 var(--rp-s4); border: 1px solid var(--rp-verified); border-radius: var(--cp-radius); background: transparent; color: var(--rp-verified); font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; cursor: pointer; }
.cp-button:hover { background: var(--rp-verified-ghost); }
.cp-button:disabled { opacity: .45; cursor: not-allowed; }
.cp-button--ghost { border-color: var(--cp-rule); color: var(--cp-ink-dim); }
```

Metrics:
```css
.cp-metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(10.5rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--rp-s3); margin: var(--rp-s4) 0 0; }
.cp-metric { border-left: 2px solid var(--cp-rule); padding-left: var(--rp-s3); }
.cp-metric dt { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .625rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); }
.cp-metric dd { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 1.125rem; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; color: var(--cp-ink); margin: 2px 0 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
```

Flags:
```css
.cp-flags { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--rp-s2); margin: var(--rp-s4) 0 0; padding: 0; }
.cp-flag { border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-radius: 999px; padding: var(--rp-s1) var(--rp-s3); font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .6875rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); }
.cp-flag--on { border-color: var(--rp-stamp); background: var(--rp-stamp-ghost); color: var(--rp-paper); }
.cp-provenance { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .6875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); margin: var(--rp-s4) 0 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.cp-provenance code { color: var(--rp-verified); font-family: inherit; }
```

Presets:
```css
.cp-presets { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(13rem, 1fr)); gap: var(--rp-s3); margin-top: var(--rp-s4); }
.cp-preset { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--rp-s1); align-items: flex-start; text-align: left; min-height: 44px; padding: var(--rp-s3); border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-radius: var(--cp-radius); background: rgba(7,12,24,.4); color: var(--cp-ink); cursor: pointer; transition: border-color 160ms ease, background-color 160ms ease; }
.cp-preset:hover { border-color: var(--rp-money); background: var(--rp-money-ghost); }
.cp-preset[aria-pressed='true'] { border-color: var(--rp-money); background: var(--rp-money-ghost); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--rp-money); }
.cp-preset__label { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: .9375rem; }
.cp-preset__card { font-size: .75rem; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); }
.cp-preset[aria-pressed='true'] .cp-preset__card { color: var(--cp-ink-dim); }
```

Twist card:
```css
.cp-twist-card { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.6vw, 1.1875rem); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--cp-ink); margin: 0; max-width: 46ch; }
```

Verdict hero:
```css
.cp-verdict { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--rp-s4); margin-top: var(--rp-s4); padding: var(--rp-s4); border: 1px solid var(--cp-rule); border-left-width: 6px; border-radius: var(--cp-radius); background: rgba(7,12,24,.55); --cp-band: var(--cp-ink-faint); }
.cp-verdict[data-band='critical'] { --cp-band: var(--cp-band-critical); }
.cp-verdict[data-band='storm_warning'] { --cp-band: var(--cp-band-storm); }
.cp-verdict[data-band='watch'] { --cp-band: var(--cp-band-watch); }
.cp-verdict[data-band='fair_skies'] { --cp-band: var(--cp-band-fair); }
.cp-verdict[data-band='clear'] { --cp-band: var(--cp-band-clear); }
.cp-verdict { border-left-color: var(--cp-band); }
.cp-verdict__glyph { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); line-height: 1; color: var(--cp-band); }
.cp-verdict__body { display: grid; gap: 2px; min-width: 0; }
.cp-verdict__caption { font-family: var(--rp-font-utility); font-size: .625rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--cp-ink-faint); }
.cp-verdict__label { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(1.125rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem); letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--cp-band); }
.cp-verdict__runway { font-family: var(--rp-font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 6vw, 4rem); line-height: 1; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; letter-spacing: -0.03em; color: var(--cp-band); }
```
Hmm: `letter-spacing: -0.03em` — negative em; fine.

Wait, the class `text-cp-critical` from band.tailwind sets color too — both set color; Tailwind utility comes later in cascade? Tailwind utilities are in @layer utilities (via @tailwind utilities at top of file), and my .cp-verdict__label is a plain rule outside layers → plain rules win over @layer rules regardless of order? In CSS cascade layers, unlayered styles have higher priority than layered ones ✓. Tailwind's utilities are in layers (base/components/utilities) → my unlayered rules win. So band.tailwind class would be overridden by .cp-verdict__label color.

That's a problem: band.tailwind must actually apply. Where do I rely on band.tailwind? In VerdictBadge I apply `${band.tailwind}` to label and runway spans. If .cp-verdict__label sets color: var(--cp-band) it overrides. The visual result is identical (same color), but the tailwind field becomes decorative.To make tailwind meaningful, I should NOT set color in .cp-verdict__label/.cp-verdict__runway (let the utility do it), and use --cp-band only for glyph/border. Then band.tailwind is the single source of color for text ✓ and the tailwind class is genuinely used (and scanned by Tailwind content ✓).

But then the compact/hero variants both rely on utility classes ✓. And if someone forgets the class, text is default ink. Fine.

So:
- .cp-verdict__label, .cp-verdict__runway: no color (inherit) but they'd inherit body color (paper) unless class applied ✓ always applied in VerdictBadge.
- glyph + border-left use --cp-band ✓ (data-band selectors).

Good, that keeps band.tailwind load-bearing.

Animation:
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .cp-verdict__runway { animation: cp-tick 320ms cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.3,1); }
}
@keyframes cp-tick { from { transform: translateY(-0.12em); opacity: .35; } to { transform: none; opacity: 1; } }
```

Compact variant smaller:
```css
.cp-verdict--compact { padding: var(--rp-s3); gap: var(--rp-s3); }
.cp-verdict--compact .cp-verdict__runway { font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); }
.cp-verdict--compact .cp-verdict__glyph { font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); }
```

Sliders:
```css
.cp-sliders { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: var(--rp-s5) 0 0; display: grid; gap: var(--rp-s4); }
.cp-sliders legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: var(--rp-s2); }
.cp-field__head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: var(--rp-s3); }
